  "scope": "Adjacent ABBA on shared Windows/Debian hosts, P0/P1 random modest policies, ten stochastic teachers and capture, four native workers, 600 warmup/1200 measured steps, explicit cap 256/batch 65536. Exact same-target state, distributions, work, capture and memory reservation are required; cross-platform bit identity is not claimed.",
  "resourceProjection": "Default aggregate observations rebuilt through a scalar/kernel-counter allowlist. GPU model names, process inventories, WSL distribution identities, commands, PIDs and private host paths are excluded.",
  "conclusion": "Both radix primitive screens are slower on ordinary random/heap keys. Packed u128 primitive keys improve isolated sorting, but complete native runs show no Windows gain and worse Debian mean service, so all candidates are rejected. Production native source remains the baseline.",
